00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:04,100
So this kind of serial cable,

122
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,720
we say it's actually very simple.

123
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,880
It's just one receive, one transmit.

124
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,780
It's this diagram here.

125
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:09,740
With this diagram added,

126
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:10,720
the meaning it actually conveys is this:

127
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,860
You can take what we just talked about on this side,

128
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,440
treat this end as this thing here,

129
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,720
and then treat this side as that thing,

130
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,420
and then the two sides are connected by one cable.

131
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:19,700
Inside this cable, actually,

132
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,240
there are actually two wires.

133
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,980
If you cut open that serial cable,

134
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:26,200
you'll find there are at least two or three wires inside.

135
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,240
So this one-receive-one-transmit,

136
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,180
that is, the TX on this side,

137
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,940
in technical terms, is the transmitting end.

138
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:33,860
That means it's for sending.

139
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,260
So the transmit side, and then over here,

140
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:38,440
this side is a receive, RX.

141
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,660
So T stands for transmit.

142
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,120
And R stands for receive.

143
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:44,700
That makes it easy to remember and understand.

144
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,800
So what it sends here,

145
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,120
comes from here to its receiving end.

146
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,340
And on this side,

147
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:51,320
if there is information,

148
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,880
you can also send information over from here.

149
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:54,460
Think about it, isn't that right?

150
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:57,400
For example, when you press Enter on your side,

151
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,260
or type some characters,

152
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:00,820
how do those characters get transmitted to this board of ours?

153
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:03,680
Well, they actually go through the transmit direction here.

154
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:07,540
So this serial port actually has two wires, one for sending and one for receiving.

155
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:09,440
It can send and receive at the same time.

156
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:15,400
Now, normally for our host machine,

